## 3. Steps to Push and Open Pull Request on GitHub

Once your fork is created:
1. Configure your origin remote:
   ```bash
   git remote set-url origin https://github.com/shravanishep/mcino-Introduction-to-Git-and-GitHub.git
   ```
2. Push your `bug-fix-revert` branch:
   ```bash
   git push -u origin bug-fix-revert
   ```
3. In GitHub, go to your repository page:
   **https://github.com/shravanishep/mcino-Introduction-to-Git-and-GitHub**
4. Click **Compare & pull request** next to `bug-fix-revert`.
5. Set:
   - **Base repository**: `ibm-developer-skills-network/mcino-Introduction-to-Git-and-GitHub` (or `shravanishep/mcino-Introduction-to-Git-and-GitHub`)
   - **Base**: `main`
   - **Head repository**: `shravanishep/mcino-Introduction-to-Git-and-GitHub`
   - **Compare**: `bug-fix-revert`
   - **Title**: `Bug fix revert`
   - **Description**: `Reverts the simple interest formula change on bug-fix-revert branch for the Coursera Git and GitHub final project.`
6. Click **Create pull request**.
   *(Note: Upstream has an automated workflow that acknowledges and closes student PRs with a congratulatory message).*

